{
  "analysis": "QEMU is running correctly with VNC on port 5901 and the monitor socket accepting `sendkey` commands. The VNC screenshot was captured successfully (720x400). However, nginx is not serving noVNC correctly because `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf` has its own inline server block on port 80 that proxies to a non-existent `127.0.0.1:8080`, and it does not include `sites-enabled/*`. The novnc site config is never loaded. We need to fix nginx.conf to serve noVNC and proxy websockify. The 720x400 resolution suggests the VM may still be in text/VGA mode and not yet at the Windows 3.11 desktop (which would typically be 640x480), so we should also wait and check the screenshot.",
  "plan": "Fix nginx.conf by replacing the inline server block with an include for sites-enabled, reload nginx, then verify the web interface. Also analyze the screenshot to check if the VM is at the desktop or still booting, and wait if needed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /etc/nginx/nginx.conf << 'NGINX'
user  root;
worker_processes  1;

events {
    worker_connections 4096;
}

http {
    include       mime.types;
    default_type  application/octet-stream;

    sendfile on;
    tcp_nopush on;
    tcp_nodelay on;

    keepalive_timeout 65;

    include /etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf;
    include /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*;
}
NGINX
nginx -t && nginx -s reload
